      'imp-917-partial-pppp (commit this commit): added scripts/imp-917-run-cell.mjs --batch-plan-cost-triple-undecmean, the shell-only undecic-mean (p=11 Kolmogorov power-mean) emitter extending the already-paired duodectet {HM (p=-1, partial-vvv/www), GM (p=0, partial-ttt/uuu), AM (p=1, partial-hhh/iii), QM (p=2, partial-xxx/yyy), CM (p=3, partial-zzz/aaaa), QUM (p=4, partial-bbbb/cccc), QIM (p=5, partial-dddd/eeee), SXM (p=6, partial-ffff/gggg), SPM (p=7, partial-hhhh/iiii), OCM (p=8, partial-jjjj/kkkk), NPM (p=9, partial-llll/mmmm), DCM (p=10, partial-nnnn/oooo)} upward to a thirteenth power-mean at p=11. Computed as UDM = (sum(wallSec_i^11) / n)^(1/11) via Math.pow(s, 1/11); by the generalized power-mean inequality UDM dominates every lower-p sibling so the full ordering UDM >= DCM >= NPM >= OCM >= SPM >= SXM >= QIM >= QUM >= CM >= QM >= AM >= GM >= HM now holds inline across all thirteen emitters. Handler uses the (((x^2)^2)^2) * (x^2) * x factorization (const w2 = r.wallSec * r.wallSec; const w4 = w2 * w2; const w8 = w4 * w4; undecSum += w8 * w2 * r.wallSec;) to avoid calling Math.pow in the inner reduce loop, matching the partial-zzz (x^2)*x cubmean / partial-dddd ((x^2)^2)*x quintmean / partial-hhhh ((x^2)^2*(x^2))*x septmean / partial-llll (((x^2)^2)^2)*x nonmean odd-exponent cadence. Odd-exponent eleventh-power preserves sign (mirroring p=3/5/7/9) but wallSec values are strictly positive by construction so no non-positive-wallSec guard is required. The only degenerate case is all-unknown (known.length === 0) which prints the dedicated "unknown" summary and exits 0 rather than (0/0)^(1/11) = NaN. Pure data emitter, exit 0 unconditionally (no validation gate), not wired into --preflight / --preflight-json. Shell-only this partial; a --batch-plan-cost-triple-undecmean-json analog can follow as partial-qqqq. Inserted the handler immediately before the existing args.batchPlanCostTripleDecmeanJson handler so the future partial-qqqq JSON handler can slot adjacent to its shell sibling mirroring the partial-nnnn/oooo decmean adjacency already on disk. Reuses computeBatchPlanCost() (partial-vv helper) with zero new batch-plan logic. Verified locally: --batch-plan-cost-triple-undecmean prints "imp-917 BATCH_PLAN per-triple undecic-mean wall-time: 65157 s (~18.10 CPU-hours) across 6 known triple(s)." with exit=0 and UDM(65157) > DCM(64509) > NPM(63726) confirms the expected p=11 > p=10 > p=9 ordering; --batch-plan-cost-triple-decmean still prints 64509 s / 17.92 CPU-hours byte-for-byte identical (refactor-invariant); --batch-plan-cost-triple-nonmean still prints 63726 s / 17.70 CPU-hours unchanged; npm run build passes in 4.58s.',
